# Internationalization (i18n) Standards

- Never hardcode user-facing strings
- Always use i18n.t() for all text strings
- Organize translation keys by screen or feature
- Use dot notation for nested translation keys
- Include all languages in translation files

## Translations Usage

```tsx
import i18n from '@/services/i18n';

// ❌ Don't do this
<Text>Welcome to the app</Text>

// ✅ Do this
<Text>{i18n.t('common.welcome')}</Text>

// ✅ With variables
<Text>{i18n.t('user.greeting', { name: username })}</Text>
```

## Translation Keys Organization

```json
{
  "common": {
    "welcome": "Welcome to the app",
    "continue": "Continue",
    "cancel": "Cancel"
  },
  "auth": {
    "login": {
      "title": "Login to your account",
      "emailPlaceholder": "Enter your email"
    }
  }
}
```
